    {
      "id": "M4114-A",
      "prompt": "A. A fictional soft sensor receives a zero-filled measurement tensor plus an observation mask. Zeros at unobserved positions are placeholders, not estimated values. A shared encoder feeds a quality predictor and, during training only, a decoder whose reconstruction loss uses observed measurements. Some quality labels are unavailable. At inference only the encoder and predictor run. The draft says: 'The network first restores all missing measurements, then fuses the reconstructed data to predict quality.' Replace this with two connected English abstract-method sentences and a brief Chinese rationale. Preserve the implemented model; no numerical performance evidence is supplied.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Connect observed-input reconstruction during training to the shared representation and sparse-label quality prediction.",
        "Retain inference encoder/predictor roles and distinguish placeholders from estimates."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent completed measurements or a serial reconstruction-fusion inference path.",
        "Claim proven recovery accuracy or eliminate the legitimate reconstruction objective."
      ],
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
