    {
      "id": "M4114-B",
      "prompt": "B. A fictional imputer uses finite placeholders and M=1 for observed inputs, with x_complete=M*x_input+(1-M)*x_hat. A downstream classifier uses x_complete. Training reconstruction error is evaluated on observed positions. For a separate test, production runs were held out before preprocessing; 10% of their observed entries were randomly hidden, excluded from the supplied input, and scored against retained reference values. All preprocessing and model choices were fixed from training data. No reference exists for naturally missing entries. Give one English contribution sentence and a concise Chinese assessment of what this evaluation supports and what it does not. The author asks whether unchanged observed values and imputation accuracy can both be discussed.",
      "required_behaviors": [
